--TEST--
A `private` class constant is read only inside its class, and a `protected` one also inside the classes that extend it — `rule:core-api/written-visibility`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `Limits` and `Strict` read both constants and give no diagnostic. `Report`
// does not extend `Limits`, and the top level is outside every class, so
// exactly two diagnostics are reported.
class Limits {
    private const int SECRET = 7;
    protected const int SHARED = 8;

    public function total(): int {
        return self::SECRET + self::SHARED;
    }
}

class Strict extends Limits {
    public function shared(): int {
        return self::SHARED + Limits::SHARED;
    }
}

class Report {
    public function show(): int {
        return Limits::SHARED;
    }
}

echo Limits::SECRET, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0471]: `Limits::SHARED` is `protected`, so only `Limits` and the classes that extend it reach it
%A
error[E0471]: `Limits::SECRET` is `private`, so only `Limits`'s own bodies reach it
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
